Sogen: a redirected stdin is a file, not the console

The guest's stdin was the console whatever the host's: FILE_TYPE_CHAR
to GetFileType, a console to GetConsoleMode. A program that reads a
console stdin with ReadConsole -- SBCL does -- reads nothing under
Sogen, whose console serves no ReadConsole, and a console has no end
of input to stop at in any case. On Windows a redirected stdin is the
file or pipe it was redirected from, read with ReadFile to its end.

nodecode's trial verb reads its form from stdin to its end, piped in
as release-windows.ps1 pipes it; under Sogen every trial waited out its
deadline with no answer, starting a thread every few seconds.

When the host's stdin is not a terminal, the guest's is now a disk file
to GetFileType and the console's requests on it fail, as they fail on a
file; its reads go through NtReadFile, which Sogen serves from the
host's stdin to its end.

diff --git a/src/emulator-platform/platform/console_backend.hpp b/src/emulator-platform/platform/console_backend.hpp
index 716843e..a17d46c 100644
--- a/src/emulator-platform/platform/console_backend.hpp
+++ b/src/emulator-platform/platform/console_backend.hpp
@@ -62,6 +62,13 @@ namespace sogen
         {
             return {};
         }
+
+        // Whether the host's stdin is a terminal; a backend that cannot tell says it is. The guest's stdin is
+        // the console only then: redirected, it is a file, which reads to an end, where a console never does.
+        virtual bool input_is_terminal() const
+        {
+            return true;
+        }
     };
 
     class null_console_backend final : public console_backend
